                "senderName": "NWS Des Moines IA",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 9 at 7:06AM CDT until September 10 at 8:00AM CDT by NWS Des Moines IA",
                "description": "...The National Weather Service in Des Moines has issued a Flood\nWatch for the following rivers in Iowa...\n\nMiddle River near Indianola affecting Warren County.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Middle River near Indianola, or from Clanton Creek near\nSpring Hill to the Des Moines River.\n\n* WHEN...From this afternoon to Thursday morning.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 6:15 AM CDT Wednesday the stage was 15.6 feet, and rising.\n- Forecast...Flood stage may be reached late this afternoon.\n- Flood stage is 23.0 feet.",
                "instruction": "For the latest stream observations and forecasts refer to\nweather.gov/desmoines/water.\n\nRiver forecasts include observed precipitation plus forecast\nprecipitation over the next 24 hours.",
